The TypeScript adaptation models only linear single-input chains, refuses any
negotiation it cannot reproduce exactly (an input trim that reorders merges, a
pick of s64/s64p) instead of approximating it, and adds no FFmpeg runtime code.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
Each audio filter added later records its own provenance in NOTICE-<NAME>.
